  external tool/library and is not vendored.
* Third-party Python and npm dependencies keep their own licences (see their packages).

InTAS-derived files tracked in this repository
----------------------------------------------
The following files are derived from the InTAS network/signal programs (lane geometry,
signal phase programs, counts). Whether such factual/geometric extracts are a "work based on"
InTAS is unsettled; to be safe, treat them as licensed under GPL-3.0 (NOT Apache-2.0):

  data/processed/network.geojson
  data/metadata/demand_metadata.json
  artifacts/scenario/*.json
  artifacts/scenario/static_programs.add.xml
  configs/sumo/InTAS_train.sumocfg   (our edit of an InTAS-style config)

Anyone who wants a fully permissive checkout can delete these and regenerate them with
src/scenario/* and scripts/generate_static_programs.py after running scripts/setup_sumo.sh.

